# Where `@cyka/ui` comes from. It is a private package in the `cykacloud`
# group's registry, so the scope needs an address and a token, and both belong
# beside the manifest that names it rather than on whatever machine happens to
# build here.
#
# **The group endpoint, not the instance one.** GitLab's instance-wide npm
# endpoint only answers for a scope spelled the same as the root namespace, and
# the scope is `@cyka` while the group is `cykacloud`.
#
# `CYKA_NPM_TOKEN` is that group's `npm read` deploy token — read on the package
# registry and nothing else — so this file holds no secret and is committed.
@cyka:registry=https://lab.cyka.cloud/api/v4/groups/cykacloud/-/packages/npm/
//lab.cyka.cloud/api/v4/groups/cykacloud/-/packages/npm/:_authToken=${CYKA_NPM_TOKEN}
